30,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The neighboring block had residents stop attending meetings due to payment disputes. We must avoid creating financial enemies.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found that the same flats have held the covered spots for years without any review. That explains the grumbling.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"It's worse than we thought. People are shifting other bikes just to leave, and some spots are completely exposed to rain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Our ledger is nearly empty; any upgrades require a levy. Meanwhile, the ward park is expensive and has a long waitlist.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The current cash collection is already a burden. Adding per-space billing would increase the treasurer's workload significantly.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, if the arrangement has been static for five years, a sudden change might be jarring. We need a smooth transition.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,But the daily riders told me they'd actually prefer to pay for a guaranteed spot than have an equal claim.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If we keep fixed spots, the ""rainy"" spots will always be the source of conflict. The physical layout is the problem.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"If residents are willing to pay, we could solve our budget issues. It's the most rational way to allocate scarce resources.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, but who manages the money? The handover file shows the current process is already tedious.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, is the physical effort of a new rack system any better?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I just want everyone to feel it's fair. A lottery might be the kindest way?,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A lottery doesn't fix the ""shoving match"" in the morning or the rain. We need a structural change.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A lottery is a gamble. Paid allocation ensures those who value the space most get it, and the building profits.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The display frame trial showed that double-tier racks are physically demanding and require regular maintenance.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"So we have a choice between administrative burden, social friction, or physical difficulty.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm worried that paying for spots might make some neighbors feel excluded.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I'm more worried about the bikes leaning on each other and the morning chaos.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be realistic. We can't afford new equipment without a levy, and we can't ignore the revenue potential.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I prefer the option with the least amount of monthly paperwork and maintenance.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A creates financial tension, B is a temporary fix, and C creates physical chaos. I lean toward B for stability.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I like B too. A lottery is fair and doesn't make people feel like they are ""buying"" a right.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I strongly oppose B. It doesn't solve the congestion. Option C, shared racks, removes the ""my spot"" mentality entirely.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is a nightmare to maintain and expensive to install. Option A is the only one that makes financial sense.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option C requires greasing and physical effort. Option A is a paperwork nightmare. Option B is the lowest maintenance.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, wouldn't shared racks just lead to more ""leaning"" and complaints since no one is responsible for a spot?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"Exactly! And if the racks are hard to use, people will just park wherever they want.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"At least it's honest. Right now, the ""covered"" spots are a hidden privilege.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, surely the benefit of a building fund outweighs a few hours of bookkeeping?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,Not if the treasurer quits. We've seen roles lapse before. I cannot support Option A.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we go with B, we reset the unfairness Yumi found without the risks of A or C.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I agree. It's a fresh start for everyone every year.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,It's a lazy solution. We are ignoring the physical congestion and the rain.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It's not lazy, it's just inefficient. We are leaving money on the table and ignoring the market value of the spaces.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Efficiency is useless if the system is unsustainable. B is the only one that doesn't create a new job.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,It seems B is the most logical compromise for social harmony.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm voting for B!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I'll stick with C, but it seems I'm outnumbered.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll vote A. I cannot support a system that ignores the financial reality.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,My vote is for B.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
